        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>For the reaction $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure on the equilibrium position?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium to the side with fewer moles of gas. Here, the left side has 4 moles (1 N<sub>2</sub> + 3 H<sub>2</sub>), and the right side has 2 moles (2 NH<sub>3</sub>). Thus, the equilibrium shifts to the right, favoring the formation of NH<sub>3</sub>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "93595",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Shifts to the left",
                "is_correct": false
