        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>For the equilibrium reaction: $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium to the side with fewer moles of gas to reduce the pressure. In this reaction, the product side (2 moles of $NH_3$) has fewer moles than the reactant side (4 moles of $N_2$ and $H_2$ combined), so the equilibrium shifts to the right, favoring the formation of $NH_3$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
